---
import { ArrowLeftIcon } from "lucide-react";

import ThemeToggle from "@/components/theme-toggle";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/base-layout.astro";

const repositoryUrl = "https://github.com/davutac/kisa";
---

<BaseLayout
  description="How Kisa accesses, stores, shares, retains, and deletes your mail data."
  title="Privacy | Kisa"
>
  <div class="page-shell relative min-h-screen overflow-x-clip">
    <header class="sticky inset-x-0 top-0 z-50" data-sticky-header>
      <div aria-hidden="true" class="header-backdrop" data-header-backdrop></div>
      <div class="relative mx-auto flex h-18 max-w-6xl items-center justify-between px-5 sm:px-8">
        <a class="flex items-center gap-2.5" href="/" aria-label="Kisa home">
          <img alt="" class="size-8 rounded-lg shadow-sm" height="32" src="/icon.png" width="32" />
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight">Kisa</span>
        </a>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
          <a class="inline-flex h-10 items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="/">
            <ArrowLeftIcon className="size-3.5" />
            Home
          </a>
          <ThemeToggle client:load />
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 pb-24 pt-16 sm:px-8 sm:pb-32 sm:pt-24">
      <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 text-balance text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.05em] sm:text-6xl">No Kisa cloud. No hidden copy.</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-pretty text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        Kisa is a local-first mail client for Gmail, iCloud, Outlook, and other IMAP accounts. It does not operate a cloud mailbox or user-account service, and your mail and credentials are not retained by a Kisa backend.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-14 divide-y border-y">
        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">What Kisa accesses</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            When you connect an account, Kisa signs in to your provider's mail servers over IMAP and SMTP and accesses the mail data needed to operate the mail client: messages, headers, participants, conversation metadata, folders and labels, attachments, and mailbox state. Kisa also keeps the email address and the optional sender name you enter. Kisa uses this data to sync, display, search, compose, send, and manage mail at your direction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">How you sign in</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Most accounts sign in with an app password, a separate password your provider issues for one app. You type it once into Kisa's Add account window; Kisa checks it against your provider's mail servers and stores it encrypted on your device.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Outlook.com and Microsoft 365 accounts sign in with Microsoft in your browser instead, so your Microsoft password never reaches Kisa. Kisa asks Microsoft only for permission to read and send your mail over IMAP and SMTP and to confirm which address signed in, and stores the resulting refresh token encrypted on your device.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Your data stays on your device</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Kisa stores your encrypted sign-in, account name and address, downloaded mail, labels, local drafts, scheduled messages, search index, account settings, and synchronization state on your device. This data persists across app restarts for as long as the account remains connected. Kisa does not upload or retain a copy on a Kisa-operated server.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Kisa connects directly to your mail provider</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            The app talks directly to your mail provider's IMAP and SMTP servers, and to Microsoft's sign-in service for Outlook accounts, to sign in, refresh access, and sync and manage your mail. Kisa does not send your mail, passwords, or tokens through a Kisa backend.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Mail actions affect your mail account</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Actions such as sending mail, changing read state or labels, starring, archiving, moving mail to Trash or Spam, and restoring mail from Spam are sent directly to your mail provider. Delete forever is available only for conversations in Spam or Trash and permanently deletes the selected conversation from your provider after you confirm the action.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">AI runs only when you ask or enable it</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            When you choose Create reply, Clean, or the manual Categorize action, Kisa sends the draft or a bounded copy of cached thread context directly to your selected AI provider: Codex, Claude Code, or a provider connected through OpenCode. Categorization also sends the account's user-created label names so the provider can select matching existing labels. If you enable automatic categorization for an account, Kisa performs that same categorization for each newly discovered conversation without a separate action. Automatic categorization is off by default and each eligible conversation is attempted once without a persistent retry queue. Kisa uses this content only to return the writing or categorization result and does not use it to train an AI model. The selected provider processes the content under the terms, retention rules, and data controls of your plan with that provider.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Kisa does not provide AI accounts or retain provider credentials. AI requests are sent directly from your device using a provider command-line tool and account configured by you. Each request runs from an empty temporary directory with provider tool access restricted, and Kisa deletes temporary request output when the operation ends. Provider-side retention and model-training behavior depend on your provider, plan, and account configuration. OpenCode can connect to different upstream providers, so the provider and model selected in your OpenCode configuration determine where that request is processed.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Retention and deletion</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            To remove an account's locally stored data, open Kisa Settings, select the account, and choose Disconnect. Kisa deletes that account's saved sign-in, downloaded mail, labels, local drafts, scheduled messages, search index, settings, synchronization state, and trusted-sender choices from the device. Attachment preview data exists only for the current app session.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Disconnecting an account does not delete mail from your provider or undo changes already sent to it; delete messages with Kisa's mail actions or directly with your provider. It also does not revoke the sign-in itself: to stop it from working, revoke the app password, or Kisa's access to your Microsoft account, in your provider's settings. Revoking access there prevents future access but does not by itself remove data already stored on your device; use Disconnect in Kisa before uninstalling when you want that local data removed.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Limited use of your mail data</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Kisa uses your mail data only to provide the user-facing mail and optional AI writing and categorization features described on this page. Kisa does not sell your data, use it for advertising, use it to determine creditworthiness, or use it to train or improve generalized AI or machine-learning models.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Independent from your mail provider</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Kisa is an independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Google, Apple, Microsoft, or any other mail provider.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Website hosting</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            Kisa does not add analytics, tracking pixels, or advertising cookies to this site. Cloudflare hosts it and processes limited technical data, such as IP addresses and request metadata, to deliver and protect it under its{" "}
            <a class="underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/policies/privacy/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>.
            Your theme preference is stored only in your browser.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="py-8">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold">Questions and requests</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
            For privacy questions or help deleting data, contact the project maintainer through the{" "}
            <a class="underline decoration-border underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground" href={repositoryUrl} rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Kisa repository</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-muted-foreground">Last updated November 25, 2026.</p>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
